2:13:23.402816"}}},"ISBN:9781563384172":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781563384172","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL8643923M/The_Cosmos_in_the_Light_of_the_Cross","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL8643923M/The_Cosmos_in_the_Light_of_the_Cross","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/1896002-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Trinity Press International"],"number_of_pages":213,"weight":"1.1 pounds","isbn_10":["1563384175"],"covers":[1896002],"physical_format":"Hardcover","key":"/books/OL8643923M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL448146A","name":"George L. Murphy"}],"subjects":["Religion & Beliefs","Religion - Theology","Person and offices","Religion","Religion and science","Christian Theology - Cosmology","Christian Theology - Soteriology","Philosophy","Jesus Christ","Christianity - Theology - Cosmology"],"isbn_13":["9781563384172"],"source_records":["marc:marc_loc_updates/v39.i41.records.utf8:3209058:914","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:32583733:5640","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part30.utf8:165907451:914","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:32596644:5640","bwb:9781563384172","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.09.20150123.full.mrc:217622551:758","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_035.bib.mrc:347937316:5057"],"title":"The Cosmos in the Light of the Cross","identifiers":{"goodreads":["3037282"],"librarything":["3197977"]},"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"local_id":["urn:cst:10017002303"],"publish_date":"November 2003","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2939012W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"8.8 x 6.9 x 0.8 inches","lccn":["2003014285"],"lc_classifications":["BL240.3 .M87 2003","BL240.3.M87 2003"],"oclc_numbers":["52559037"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"In The Cosmos in the Light of the Cross, George Murphy finds understanding in the theology of the cross, with a God who becomes a participant in the universe and thereby shares the suffering, loss, and death that are part of the worldly experience. Jesus is willing to be condemned in the name of the law, to be rejected and abandoned by humanity, and to be abandoned even by God. What is supposed to be the saving act of God is an action in which God seems to be completely absent, for nothing seems less like the presence of an all-powerful and loving God than this scene in which a Jewish carpenter hangs as a dead criminal on a Roman cross.\" \"Murphy uses this theology of the cross as a perspective form which to read ecology, evolution, and bioethics. His view gives us new opportunities to understand the apparent absence of God in natural processes, the role of death in evolution, and the ethical ambiguities raised by science-based technologies.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":13,"revision":13,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T08:14:56.482104"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-04-27T02:41:45.573955"}}},"ISBN:9780802847584":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780802847584","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7904162M/The_Depth_of_the_Riches_A_Trinitarian_Theology_of_Religious_Ends_(Sacra_Doctrina_Christian_Theology_","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL7904162M/The_Depth_of_the_Riches_A_Trinitarian_Theology_of_Religious_Ends_(Sacra_Doctrina_Christian_Theology_","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/573025-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["Wm. B. Eerdmans Publishing Company"],"number_of_pages":312,"weight":"1.4 pounds","isbn_10":["0802847587"],"covers":[573025],"local_id":["urn:cst:10011458422","urn:scms:0188600232105","urn:bwbsku:KS-055-723","urn:bwbsku:S0-BAP-490"],"physical_format":"Hardcover","key":"/books/OL7904162M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL446050A","name":"S. Mark Heim"}],"contributions":["Alan G. Padgett (Editor)"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"first_sentence":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The most rigid liberal and conservative theological approaches share a largely undefended assumption that there is and can be only one religious end, one actual religious fulfillment."},"source_records":["marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_barcode.mrc:15265984:3881","marc:marc_loc_2016/BooksAll.2016.part01.utf8:45054383:751","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC2_multibarcode.mrc:15273379:3881","bwb:9780802847584","marc:marc_scms/20220805_ADAM_MARC_records.mrc:46135913:1666","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-010.mrc:35371875:1234","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2023-05-16:KS-055-723","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2024-11-06:S0-BAP-490","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_021.bib.mrc:212669939:2690"],"title":"The Depth of the Riches: A Trinitarian Theology of Religious Ends (Sacra Doctrina: Christian Theology for a Postmodern Age)","lccn":["00063666"],"identifiers":{"goodreads":["264254"],"librarything":["626838"]},"isbn_13":["9780802847584"],"subjects":["Christian theology","Nature & existence of God","Religion","God (Theology)","Theology - Academic","Trinity","Theology of religions (Christian theology)","Christian Theology - Anthropology","Ecumenism","Pluralism","Christianity - Theology - General","Christian Theology - General","Theology of religions (Christi"],"publish_date":"February 2001","works":[{"key":"/works/OL2926756W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"physical_dimensions":"9.4 x 6.3 x 0.8 inches","lc_classifications":["BT83.85 .H45 2001","BT83.85.H45 2001","BT 83.85 .H45 2001"],"oclc_numbers":["44818323"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"\"In this work S. Mark Heim probes the Christian understanding of God and salvation and offers a new perspective on religious pluralism that recognizes different religious ends in other faiths. The questions explored here are both difficult and enlightening. What is the distinctive nature of salvation? Is there a place in Christian theology for recognizing other religious ends in addition to salvation? In pursuit of meaningful answers, Heim uses the classical doctrine of the Trinity to develop a theology that respects the possibility that alternative relations with God exist in other religions.\"--BOOK JACKET."},"latest_revision":16,"revision":16,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-29T15:03:11.581851"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2025-11-11T12:33:19.007924"}}},"ISBN:9780281045754":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9780281045754","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL10290928M/A_Gentle_Touch","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL10290928M/A_Gentle_Touch","thumbnail_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/13660958-S.jpg","details":{"publishers":["SPCK Publishing","SPCK (Society for Promoting Ch"],"number_of_pages":196,"local_id":["urn:cst:10011431401","urn:bwbsku:KT-648-978"],"physical_format":"Paperback","key":"/books/OL10290928M","authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL495233A","name":"David A. Pailin"}],"subjects":["Personal Christian testimony & popular inspirational works","Christian social thought & activity","Christianity"],"source_records":["marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_barcode.mrc:201961633:2051","marc:marc_claremont_school_theology/CSTMARC1_multibarcode.mrc:202222576:2051","bwb:9780281045754","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-009.mrc:496662197:1257","amazon:0281045755","promise:bwb_daily_pallets_2024-01-08:KT-648-978","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/ab.bib.02.20150123.full.mrc:549085121:741"],"title":"A Gentle Touch","identifiers":{"goodreads":["5923311"]},"isbn_13":["9780281045754"],"isbn_10":["0281045755"],"publish_date":"May 28, 1992","oclc_numbers":["27975341","60094542","26122044"],"works":[{"key":"/works/OL3131443W"}],"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"lc_classifications":["BT702 .P340 1992","BT732.7 .P355 1992"],"covers":[13660958],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"latest_revision":12,"revision":12,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2008-04-30T09:38:13.731961"},"last_modified":